    "body": "**Problem:** Repeated boolean checks on long zero prefixes can make a valid block expensive to validate.\nFor a nearly full block that repeatedly checks 519 zero bytes followed by `01`, median `submitblock` time on a Rpi4 fell from ~3.9 s to ~1.6 s (including RPC transfer and validation).\nThe spending transaction is nonstandard, but a miner could include it directly.\n\n**Fix:** Skip leading zero bytes in 64-bit chunks with `ReadLE64`, keeping the byte checks that handle negative zero.\nThe idea is similar to [the multi-byte XOR processing in #31144](https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/31144) and follows up on [#36878](https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/36878).\nIt also adds cases around the 8-byte boundaries to the existing script test vectors.\n\n**Benchmarks:**\n\n```text\nVerifyIfDupVerifyFullLast\n  Before ████████████████████████ 3.4 s\n  After  ████████                 1.1 s\n\nVerifyIfDupFullZero\n  Before ████████████████████████ 3.3 s\n  After  ███████                  1.0 s\n\nVerifyIfDupFullNegativeZero\n  Before ████████████████████████ 3.3 s\n  After  ███████                  1.0 s\n\nVerifyIfDupVerifyFullZeroLastWord\n  Before ████████████████████████ 3.3 s\n  After  ███████                  1.0 s\n```\n\n`VerifyNestedIfScript` is roughly ~1% slower while `VerifyIfDupVerifyFullFirst`, `VerifyIfDupVerifyTrue`, `VerifyScriptP2WPKH`, `VerifyScriptP2TR_KeyPath` and `VerifyScriptP2TR_ScriptPath` are effectively unchanged.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Manual benchmark patch</summary>\n\n```diff\ndiff --git a/src/bench/verify_script.cpp b/src/bench/verify_script.cpp\n--- a/src/bench/verify_script.cpp\n+++ b/src/bench/verify_script.cpp\n@@ -5,6 +5,7 @@\n #include <addresstype.h>\n #include <bench/bench.h>\n #include <coins.h>\n+#include <consensus/consensus.h>\n #include <key.h>\n #include <policy/policy.h>\n #include <primitives/transaction.h>\n@@ -22,6 +23,7 @@\n #include <util/translation.h>\n \n #include <cstddef>\n+#include <cstdint>\n #include <map>\n #include <span>\n #include <vector>\n@@ -131,6 +133,60 @@ static void VerifyNestedIfScript(benchmark::Bench& bench)\n         });\n }\n \n+//! Maximum-size stack element that is zero except for `byte` at `pos`\n+static std::vector<uint8_t> FullElement(size_t pos, uint8_t byte)\n+{\n+    std::vector<uint8_t> value(MAX_SCRIPT_ELEMENT_SIZE);\n+    value.at(pos) = byte;\n+    return value;\n+}\n+static constexpr size_t LAST_BYTE{MAX_SCRIPT_ELEMENT_SIZE - 1};\n+\n+// A single tapscript can occupy nearly the entire block weight budget\n+// Both patterns cast the element to bool about once per opcode byte\n+static void VerifyIfDupBench(benchmark::Bench& bench, const std::vector<uint8_t>& value, bool truthy = true)\n+{\n+    constexpr uint32_t SCRIPT_SIZE{MAX_BLOCK_WEIGHT - 4000};\n+    CScript script;\n+    script.reserve(SCRIPT_SIZE);\n+    if (truthy) {\n+        for (uint32_t i{0}; i < SCRIPT_SIZE / 2; ++i) {\n+            script << OP_IFDUP << OP_VERIFY;\n+        }\n+    } else {\n+        script.insert(script.end(), SCRIPT_SIZE - 2, OP_IFDUP);\n+        script << OP_DROP << OP_1;\n+    }\n+    TaprootBuilder builder;\n+    builder.Add(0, script, TAPROOT_LEAF_TAPSCRIPT).Finalize(XOnlyPubKey::NUMS_H);\n+    const CScript script_pub_key{GetScriptForDestination(builder.GetOutput())};\n+    const auto spend_data{builder.GetSpendData()};\n+    CScriptWitness witness;\n+    witness.stack = {value, ToByteVector(script), *spend_data.scripts.begin()->second.begin()};\n+    assert(script.size() == SCRIPT_SIZE);\n+    assert(value.size() <= MAX_SCRIPT_ELEMENT_SIZE);\n+\n+    bench.unit(\"script\").run([&] {\n+        ScriptError error;\n+        const bool success{VerifyScript({}, script_pub_key, &witness, STANDARD_SCRIPT_VERIFY_FLAGS, BaseSignatureChecker(), &error)};\n+        assert(success && error == SCRIPT_ERR_OK);\n+    });\n+}\n+\n+static void VerifyIfDupVerifyFullLast(benchmark::Bench& bench) { VerifyIfDupBench(bench, FullElement(LAST_BYTE, 1)); }\n+static void VerifyIfDupVerifyFullFirst(benchmark::Bench& bench) { VerifyIfDupBench(bench, FullElement(0, 1)); }\n+static void VerifyIfDupVerifyFullZeroLastWord(benchmark::Bench& bench) { VerifyIfDupBench(bench, FullElement(LAST_BYTE - sizeof(uint64_t), 1)); }\n+static void VerifyIfDupVerifyTrue(benchmark::Bench& bench) { VerifyIfDupBench(bench, {1}); }\n+static void VerifyIfDupFullZero(benchmark::Bench& bench) { VerifyIfDupBench(bench, FullElement(0, 0), /*truthy=*/false); }\n+static void VerifyIfDupFullNegativeZero(benchmark::Bench& bench) { VerifyIfDupBench(bench, FullElement(LAST_BYTE, 0x80), /*truthy=*/false); }\n+\n+BENCHMARK(VerifyIfDupVerifyFullLast);\n+BENCHMARK(VerifyIfDupVerifyFullFirst);\n+BENCHMARK(VerifyIfDupVerifyFullZeroLastWord);\n+BENCHMARK(VerifyIfDupVerifyTrue);\n+BENCHMARK(VerifyIfDupFullZero);\n+BENCHMARK(VerifyIfDupFullNegativeZero);\n+\n BENCHMARK(VerifyScriptP2WPKH);\n BENCHMARK(VerifyScriptP2TR_KeyPath);\n BENCHMARK(VerifyScriptP2TR_ScriptPath);\n```\n</details>\n",
