      "verification": {
        "verified": true,
        "reason": "valid",
        "payload": "tree 617d4e267f233c95efcf972fbb1055c697be2a93\nparent 8456412c9d4ca8e22389a6290ae003a4b826b95c\nauthor Lőrinc <pap.lorinc@gmail.com> 1794898121 +0100\ncommitter Lőrinc <pap.lorinc@gmail.com> 1794901981 +0100\n\nscript: reduce worst-case boolean scan time\n\nRepeated boolean checks on long zero prefixes can make a valid block expensive to validate.\nSkip leading zero bytes in 64-bit chunks, keeping the byte checks that handle negative zero.\n\nFor a nearly full block that repeatedly checks 519 zero bytes followed by `01`, median `submitblock` time on a Raspberry Pi 4 fell from ~3.9 s to ~1.6 s (including RPC transfer and validation).\nThe spending transaction is nonstandard, but a miner could include it directly.\n\nThis follows up on #36878.\n\nCo-authored-by: jrakibi <j.errakibi@gmail.com>\n",
        "signature": "-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niJEEABYKADkWIQQiU97U54YbP0PlTVgnCd/LLYEwhwUCavwH3RsUgAAAAAAEAA5t\nYW51MiwyLjUrMS4xMiwwLDMACgkQJwnfyy2BMIeieQEA7ytEqiOiOrgjweHxvLVb\naNd5tV0KDLBuzDtOEYUjx8MA/iyHiNtYMAoujVogFy8DSxJTRziRjIVlG986EOGX\nuPkP\n=fa0R\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----"
