      ],
      "message": "script: reduce worst-case boolean scan time\n\nRepeated boolean checks on long zero prefixes can make a valid block expensive to validate.\nSkip leading zero bytes in 64-bit chunks, keeping the byte checks that handle negative zero.\n\nFor a nearly full block that repeatedly checks 519 zero bytes followed by `01`, median `submitblock` time on a Raspberry Pi 4 fell from ~3.9 s to ~1.6 s (including RPC transfer and validation).\nThe spending transaction is nonstandard, but a miner could include it directly.\n\nThis follows up on #36878.\n\nCo-authored-by: jrakibi <j.errakibi@gmail.com>",
